<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc Rorer launches Zagam in U.S.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer launches Zagam in U.S.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc said Monday that Zagam tablets, a once-daily oral antibiotic for the treatment of community-acquired pneumonia and acute bacterial exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, is now available by prescription nationwide.</p>
<p>The company said that Zagam recently received clearance for marketing from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.</p>
</text>
